Description: use PyGObject enum names instead of the removed value_name/value_nick
 PyGObject 3.56 replaced its GEnum wrapper with real Python enums, so enum
 members no longer expose the value_name and value_nick attributes that
 MyPaint 2.0.1 uses for logging, drag-and-drop targets and device settings
 keys. lib.glib.init_user_dir_caches() hits this on every start, which makes
 the application abort with an AttributeError before a window is shown.
 Enum members still have .name, which carries the same upper-case constant
 name for all of the affected enums (GLib.UserDirectory, Gdk.InputSource,
 Gdk.GrabStatus, Gdk.EventType and Gtk.TreeViewDropPosition); the values are
 only used for messages and for building persisted preference keys.
Origin: local
Forwarded: not-needed

